  "id": "discriminative-response",
  "term": "discriminative response",
  "definition": "A discriminative response is an action made selectively, only when a stimulus matches a required condition rather than on every trial. In the study context, it meant responding only to a moving stimulus headed toward a pre-defined target area, adding a decision about whether to act.",
